# Line endings for the bytes that leave this repository (DECISIONS.md D-0035,
# row D9).
#
# The scope is what `files` packs, because that is what a rebuilt `npm pack` has
# to reproduce byte for byte: `dist/`, `src/`, `README.md`, `LICENSE`, and the
# `package.json` npm packs alongside them. Without an attribute, a clone under
# `core.autocrlf=true` writes CRLF and packs different bytes than a Linux clone
# does, with no compiler involved at all -- and under the bridge's rebuilding
# variant a one-byte difference is `EINTEGRITY` on a correct tree. `eol=lf`
# makes the working tree LF on every platform, so a rebuilt tarball is the same
# tarball. `tsconfig.build.json` pins the other half, the compiler's own emit,
# with `newLine: "lf"`.
#
# `dist/` is gitignored today and the rule is therefore inert for it; it is
# written because the emitted tree is the other half of the same question, and a
# route that ever tracks build output must not have to remember this.
src/** text eol=lf
dist/** text eol=lf
README.md text eol=lf
LICENSE text eol=lf
package.json text eol=lf
